📘 Product Requirements Document
Product: OEM Accessory Pricing Extraction Pipeline
Status: Final (Production‑Ready)
Audience: Engineering, Analytics, Product, Data Governance

1. Executive Summary
   This pipeline ingests OEM Excel accessory pricing files and produces a clean, normalized, analysis‑ready dataset per model.
   It is designed to handle:

Inconsistent worksheet naming
Multi‑row headers
Dynamic trim applicability columns
Section‑specific formatting
Pricing continuity across rows

The system enforces strict data integrity guarantees, provides full auditability, and preserves business semantics required for downstream operations such as trim‑level record explosion.

2. Goals & Non‑Goals
   Goals

Preserve all business‑meaningful pricing and applicability data
Prevent silent data loss or duplication
Produce deterministic, explainable outputs
Support future trim‑level expansion

Non‑Goals

Inferring applicability where not explicitly provided
Normalizing model naming conventions
Pricing calculations or business rule application

3. Inputs & Outputs
   Inputs

Excel workbooks (.xlsx, .xlsm)
English worksheet only (\*\_APP_EN)
Multiple accessory sections per file

Outputs

One merged DataFrame per model
Stable schema with core + dynamic columns

4. Core Schema Contract
   Core Columns (Invariant)
   description
   part number
   dealer net
   list price
   frt
   installed price
   comments

These columns:
Must exist
Must never be dropped
Must not be empty (except comments)

5. Dynamic Columns & Applicability

Dynamic columns represent trim applicability
Valid values:
• T E S or empty

Empty means “does not apply”
No inference or auto‑population is allowed

A dynamic column is kept only if it contains ≥2 distinct applicability states.

6. Header Processing

Header row detected by presence of all core columns
Helper row used to fill missing header labels only
Helper row removed from data
Header promotion is guarded against data loss

7. Row Processing Rules
   Forward‑Fill

Applies only to core/pricing columns
Never applies to dynamic columns

Row Authority

Pricing identity defines row uniqueness:
description
part number
dealer net
list price
frt
installed price

Rows with same identity + same applicability are duplicates
Rows with same description/part number but different pricing are valid

8. Merge Strategy

Sections concatenated first
Columns reordered after concat
No column re-indexing
Dynamic columns preserved across sections

9. Data Integrity Guarantees
   The pipeline guarantees:

✅ No silent data loss
✅ No inferred applicability
✅ No duplicate pricing rows
✅ No empty pricing fields
✅ Fully auditable transformations

Failures are fail‑fast and explainable.

10. Audit & QA Strategy

The pipeline includes:
Structural validation
Header guards
Column‑level audits
Row‑level authority tracing
Merge safety checks
Final schema validation

Audits can be enabled selectively per model or section.

11. Known Constraints

Worksheet naming conventions vary (handled via relaxed regex)
Section presence may vary by model
Some parts legitimately repeat with different pricing

12. Future Extensions

Trim‑level record explosion
Export to downstream systems
Model normalization layer
Automated regression tests from audit rules

